A||||19||Adrift||No response when key turned, where to start trouble shooting?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-05-2001||12:49 PM||||I turn the key, and I hear a single "click" but get no electrical response whatsoever. I brought the battery into be checked they said it was fine. I plugged in a portable booster to the battery and tried starting it but still got the same response (nothing!). I checked all the fueses and they're fine. What should I do now? I really need to get this car running!||||reg||1
Z||000001||blazin'||11-05-2001||12:52 PM||||I was looking at a junked fiero for a parts car, and the guy said it had a rebuilt 2.5. I got him to start it and it did the same thing...He said the starter was froze...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-05-2001||01:03 PM||||Its cold, but not freezing yet... any more ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000003||K2m4||11-05-2001||01:07 PM||||When he says the starter is frozen , he means its seized. The click your hearing is the Starter solenoid engaging but your starter has ****  the bed!! Its easy to replace just a pain!...Good luck<P>Kerm<BR>86 2m4<BR>86 GT<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000004||Adrift||11-05-2001||01:26 PM||||is there any way to check if it is the starter that has crapped out? (How can I MAKE SURE its the starter?)||||reg||1
Z||000005||U Wanna Race||11-05-2001||01:55 PM||||No accesories come on right?  If no accesories come on then it sounds like your problem isnt just the starter.  ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Adrift||11-05-2001||03:01 PM||||NOTHING comes on! NOTHING happens!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jncomutt||11-05-2001||04:20 PM||||I guess this doesn't apply to your car, because you said you have no lights or anything.<P>What I do know is that when I first bought my 86 --5 speed-- it didn't start.  Everything else worked though.  I thought it could have been the starter.  What it actually was however, was that the plastic clip that goes into the clutch pedal was broken off.  Its the plastic switch for that safety thing so the clutch has to be depressed for the car to start.  Well instead of worrying about it, I went to radio shack and bought a push button type switch.  Wired it up to the "blank" below the power trunk release (I don't have rear defrost) and it makes a cheap ignition switch.  Just a lil future reference incase anyone else ever checks back at this post.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroPerformance||11-05-2001||04:28 PM||||Check your ground wire.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||11-05-2001||06:34 PM||||Fusible link.  Check all the connections on the starter, and the wires too.  One is probably broken.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Adrift||11-06-2001||12:34 AM||||Where's the ground wire located?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||11-06-2001||08:56 AM||||Also, have someone look at your headlights when you try to start the car.  If they dim a lot, you're starter is likely getting power and is just seized.  If they don't dim, you're probably not getting power to the starter and it could be a bad ground or fusible link.<P>Also, you can take the starter off and take it to most auto parts stores and they'll test it for you.  I know Advance Auto does this, I'm pretty sure most others do too.||||reg||6
Z||000012||Indyrestoguy_JR||11-06-2001||09:26 AM||||If you have absolutely no power, check your battery and ALL battery connections at BOTH ends of the BIG red and black wires that connect to it. The BLACK one should be the ground wire.||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||11-06-2001||11:36 AM||||I agree with Indyresto Jr. <BR>Every once in a while the battery terminals on my '86SE become loose, and the car will be unresponsive when I go to start up. Wiggle the connections and see if that helps too.<BR>Good luck!||||reg||7
Z||000014||fotofrank||11-06-2001||04:27 PM||||My '84 SE does the same thing. However the accesories work and the idiot lights on the das work. I turn the key and nada. However the mystery continues, when this happened ,in mt garage, it wouldn't start all day. late that night when I took the garbage out the car started. I drove it and srarted it about 6 times. Then bank it would not start. My son and I varified the started motor works (jumpered directly from the battery to it and the starter motor ran. After that we tried starting again and o-boy it started. <BR>I think I have a poor connection or the solinoid is sticking. The starter was replaced about 5 months ago. Good luck.<BR>If the check engin light comes on the electrical system from the battery on may be good. If not check the connection at the altinator,starter and for a short by removing the hot side wire from the battery and install a light bulb between the battery and disconnected battery wire. If the bulb glow you have a short. Pull fuses one at a time till you find the curcuit that is shorted and draining your battery.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||11
Z||000015||rogergarrison||11-06-2001||05:09 PM||||Id chk out the battery cables/connections, and the fusible link by the battery. Also swing down the fuse panel by the steering column and see if its hot on the backside.<BR>if theres no power anywhere, has to be one of those.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Brandon86SE||11-06-2001||05:34 PM||||Ya, I had the same thing happen to me right after I installed my amp for my car stereo.  I just checked the battery post, and tightened it up a bit more.  No problems since.  It's gotta be either a bad ground, or power connection to the battery if absolutely nothing's working.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fierochic88||11-07-2001||08:34 PM||||I'd go with Battery - happened to my sis' car and it was bad cables.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/Fierochic88Signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Adrift||11-08-2001||12:37 AM||||Well I went out and bought a wire brush and spent twenty minutes scrubing the posts on the cables and on the battery... Hooked it all back together and BAM! the car starts! You have no idea (well I gues a lot of you actually do) how my heart jumped, as if I had just saved a life! <BR>I haven't had the engine running for more then a few seconds, but this is the first step - thank you all!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Brandon86SE||11-08-2001||01:50 AM||||hurrah!  Good to hear it worked out so well for ya!<P>Brandon||||reg||10
